  "summary_en": "Chile's first National AI Policy (MinCiencia, 2021) sets a goal of leading Latin America in AI by 2031. It rests on four principles and three axes: enabling factors (talent, infrastructure, data), development and adoption, and ethics/legal/socioeconomic aspects. Largely innovation-oriented; embodied AI appears only in passing (autonomous vehicles, robotics education).",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Objective: Chile above the OECD average and the most advanced in Latin America in AI by 2031",
   "Four cross-cutting principles: human well-being and rights, sustainable development, inclusive AI, globalized AI",
   "Update personal data protection law, drawing on GDPR",
   "Create an agile institutional framework for responsible AI, avoiding over-regulation",
   "Review existing regulation affecting fundamental rights and align with the OECD and UNESCO principles"
